{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01EmbhhuEpuadmHTFLGhebRF","type":"tool_result","content":"int circle_collide(float x, float y, float r);\n=== RUST ===\n     1\t//! Rust translation of the C library in `c_src/`.\n     2\t//!\n     3\t//! Original C sources: `c_src/include/lib.h`, `c_src/src/lib.c`\n     4\t//! (a trimmed-down slice of `cute_c2` by Randy Gaul — zlib / Unlicense).\n     5\t//!\n     6\t//! The whole public ABI of the C shared object is reproduced here, symbol for\n     7\t//! symbol:\n     8\t//!\n     9\t//! ```text\n    10\t//! c2V  c2Mulvs  c2Maxv  c2Minv  c2Clampv  c2Sub  c2Dot\n    11\t//! c2CircletoCircle  c2CircletoAABB  c2CircletoCapsule\n    12\t//! c2Collided  circle_collide\n    13\t//! ```\n    14\t//!\n    15\t//! Notes on faithfulness:\n    16\t//! * All arithmetic is done in `f32`, matching C `float` on x86-64 (SSE, no\n    17\t//!   excess precision), so results are bit-for-bit identical.\n    18\t//! * The min/max helpers reproduce C's `a > b ? a : b` ternaries verbatim\n    19\t//!   rather than using `f32::max`/`f32::min`, because the two disagree on NaN\n    20\t//!   and signed zero.\n    21\t//! * No bugs are \"fixed\": e.g. `c2CircletoCapsule` still divides by\n    22\t//!   `c2Dot(n, n)` without a zero check, and `c2Collided` still blindly\n    23\t//!   reinterprets `A` as a `c2Circle`.\n    24\t\n    25\t#![allow(non_snake_case)]\n    26\t#![allow(non_camel_case_types)]\n    27\t\n    28\tuse core::ffi::{c_int, c_void};\n    29\t\n    30\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    31\t// Types (from c_src/src/lib.c)\n    32\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    33\t\n    34\t/// `typedef enum { C2_TYPE_CIRCLE, C2_TYPE_AABB, C2_TYPE_CAPSULE } C2_TYPE;`\n    35\t///\n    36\t/// A C enum whose enumerators all fit in `int` is passed as `int`, so the\n    37\t/// public entry point takes a `c_int` and compares against these constants.\n    38\tpub const C2_TYPE_CIRCLE: c_int = 0;\n    39\tpub const C2_TYPE_AABB: c_int = 1;\n    40\tpub const C2_TYPE_CAPSULE: c_int = 2;\n    41\t\n    42\t/// `typedef struct c2v { float x; float y; } c2v;`\n    43\t#[repr(C)]\n    44\t#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\n    45\tpub struct c2v {\n    46\t    pub x: f32,\n    47\t    pub y: f32,\n    48\t}\n    49\t\n    50\t/// `typedef struct c2Circle { c2v p; float r; } c2Circle;`\n    51\t#[repr(C)]\n    52\t#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\n    53\tpub struct c2Circle {\n    54\t    pub p: c2v,\n    55\t    pub r: f32,\n    56\t}\n    57\t\n    58\t/// `typedef struct c2AABB { c2v min; c2v max; } c2AABB;`\n    59\t#[repr(C)]\n    60\t#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\n    61\tpub struct c2AABB {\n    62\t    pub min: c2v,\n    63\t    pub max: c2v,\n    64\t}\n    65\t\n    66\t/// `typedef struct c2Capsule { c2v a; c2v b; float r; } c2Capsule;`\n    67\t#[repr(C)]\n    68\t#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\n    69\tpub struct c2Capsule {\n    70\t    pub a: c2v,\n    71\t    pub b: c2v,\n    72\t    pub r: f32,\n    73\t}\n    74\t\n    75\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    76\t// Bit-exact float multiply helpers\n    77\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    78\t//\n    79\t// IEEE-754 does not specify *which* NaN a binary operation returns, and on SSE\n    80\t// the answer is \"the destination operand, if it is a NaN, otherwise the source\n    81\t// operand\". So when both multiplicands are NaNs with different sign bits or\n    82\t// payloads, the raw result bytes depend on the operand order the compiler\n    83\t// happened to emit.\n    84\t//\n    85\t// `fmul` is commutative in LLVM IR, so plain `a * b` in Rust lets the backend\n    86\t// pick either order — and it picks the opposite of GCC's choice in `c2Dot` and\n    87\t// `c2Mulvs`. These helpers pin the order down to match the C shared object\n    88\t// byte for byte. Everything else in this file is ordinary `f32` arithmetic.\n    89\t\n    90\t/// `mulss dst, src` with `dst = a`: propagates `a`'s NaN in preference to `b`'s.\n    91\t///\n    92\t/// Matches GCC's `mulss %xmm(b),%xmm(a)` in `c2Dot`.\n    93\t///\n    94\t/// This has to be inline assembly: the `_mm_mul_ss` intrinsic lowers to an\n    95\t/// ordinary commutative LLVM `fmul`, which the backend then re-commutes right\n    96\t/// back to the order we are trying to avoid.\n    97\t#[cfg(target_arch = \"x86_64\")]\n    98\t#[inline(always)]\n    99\tfn mul_keep_lhs_nan(a: f32, b: f32) -> f32 {\n   100\t    let mut dst = a;\n   101\t    // SAFETY: `mulss` on two SSE registers has no memory or flag effects, and\n   102\t    // SSE is a baseline feature of the x86_64 target.\n   103\t    unsafe {\n   104\t        core::arch::asm!(\n   105\t            \"mulss {dst}, {src}\",\n   106\t            dst = inout(xmm_reg) dst,\n   107\t            src = in(xmm_reg) b,\n   108\t            options(pure, nomem, nostack, preserves_flags),\n   109\t        );\n   110\t    }\n   111\t    dst\n   112\t}\n   113\t\n   114\t#[cfg(not(target_arch = \"x86_64\"))]\n   115\t#[inline(always)]\n   116\tfn mul_keep_lhs_nan(a: f32, b: f32) -> f32 {\n   117\t    a * b\n   118\t}\n   119\t\n   120\t/// `addss dst, src` with `dst = a`: propagates `a`'s NaN in preference to `b`'s.\n   121\t///\n   122\t/// Matches GCC's `addss %xmm(b),%xmm(a)` in `c2Dot`.\n   123\t#[cfg(target_arch = \"x86_64\")]\n   124\t#[inline(always)]\n   125\tfn add_keep_lhs_nan(a: f32, b: f32) -> f32 {\n   126\t    let mut dst = a;\n   127\t    // SAFETY: `addss` on two SSE registers has no memory or flag effects, and\n   128\t    // SSE is a baseline feature of the x86_64 target.\n   129\t    unsafe {\n   130\t        core::arch::asm!(\n   131\t            \"addss {dst}, {src}\",\n   132\t            dst = inout(xmm_reg) dst,\n   133\t            src = in(xmm_reg) b,\n   134\t            options(pure, nomem, nostack, preserves_flags),\n   135\t        );\n   136\t    }\n   137\t    dst\n   138\t}\n   139\t\n   140\t#[cfg(not(target_arch = \"x86_64\"))]\n   141\t#[inline(always)]\n   142\tfn add_keep_lhs_nan(a: f32, b: f32) -> f32 {\n   143\t    a + b\n   144\t}\n   145\t\n   146\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   147\t// Vector helpers\n   148\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   149\t\n   150\t/// ```c\n   151\t/// c2v c2V(float x, float y) {\n   152\t///     c2v a;\n   153\t///     a.x = x;\n   154\t///     a.y = y;\n   155\t///     return a;\n   156\t/// }\n   157\t/// ```\n   158\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   159\tpub extern \"C\" fn c2V(x: f32, y: f32) -> c2v {\n   160\t    let mut a = c2v { x: 0.0, y: 0.0 };\n   161\t    a.x = x;\n   162\t    a.y = y;\n   163\t    a\n   164\t}\n   165\t\n   166\t/// ```c\n   167\t/// c2v c2Mulvs(c2v a, float b) {\n   168\t///     a.x *= b;\n   169\t///     a.y *= b;\n   170\t///     return a;\n   171\t/// }\n   172\t/// ```\n   173\t///\n   174\t/// GCC vectorises this to `mulps %xmm(a),%xmm(bbbb)` — i.e. the *broadcast\n   175\t/// scalar* is the destination, so `b`'s NaN wins over `a`'s in both lanes.\n   176\t/// `mul_keep_lhs_nan(b, ...)` reproduces that.\n   177\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   178\tpub extern \"C\" fn c2Mulvs(a: c2v, b: f32) -> c2v {\n   179\t    let mut a = a;\n   180\t    a.x = mul_keep_lhs_nan(b, a.x);\n   181\t    a.y = mul_keep_lhs_nan(b, a.y);\n   182\t    a\n   183\t}\n   184\t\n   185\t/// ```c\n   186\t/// c2v c2Maxv(c2v a, c2v b) {\n   187\t///     return c2V(((a.x) > (b.x) ? (a.x) : (b.x)),\n   188\t///             ((a.y) > (b.y) ? (a.y) : (b.y)));\n   189\t/// }\n   190\t/// ```\n   191\t///\n   192\t/// Deliberately *not* `f32::max`: C's ternary yields `b` when the comparison is\n   193\t/// unordered (NaN) and does not canonicalise `-0.0`/`+0.0`.\n   194\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   195\tpub extern \"C\" fn c2Maxv(a: c2v, b: c2v) -> c2v {\n   196\t    c2V(\n   197\t        if a.x > b.x { a.x } else { b.x },\n   198\t        if a.y > b.y { a.y } else { b.y },\n   199\t    )\n   200\t}\n   201\t\n   202\t/// ```c\n   203\t/// c2v c2Minv(c2v a, c2v b) {\n   204\t///     return c2V(((a.x) < (b.x) ? (a.x) : (b.x)),\n   205\t///             ((a.y) < (b.y) ? (a.y) : (b.y)));\n   206\t/// }\n   207\t/// ```\n   208\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   209\tpub extern \"C\" fn c2Minv(a: c2v, b: c2v) -> c2v {\n   210\t    c2V(\n   211\t        if a.x < b.x { a.x } else { b.x },\n   212\t        if a.y < b.y { a.y } else { b.y },\n   213\t    )\n   214\t}\n   215\t\n   216\t/// ```c\n   217\t/// c2v c2Clampv(c2v a, c2v lo, c2v hi) {\n   218\t///     return c2Maxv(lo, c2Minv(a, hi));\n   219\t/// }\n   220\t/// ```\n   221\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   222\tpub extern \"C\" fn c2Clampv(a: c2v, lo: c2v, hi: c2v) -> c2v {\n   223\t    c2Maxv(lo, c2Minv(a, hi))\n   224\t}\n   225\t\n   226\t/// ```c\n   227\t/// c2v c2Sub(c2v a, c2v b) {\n   228\t///     a.x -= b.x;\n   229\t///     a.y -= b.y;\n   230\t///     return a;\n   231\t/// }\n   232\t/// ```\n   233\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   234\tpub extern \"C\" fn c2Sub(a: c2v, b: c2v) -> c2v {\n   235\t    let mut a = a;\n   236\t    a.x -= b.x;\n   237\t    a.y -= b.y;\n   238\t    a\n   239\t}\n   240\t\n   241\t/// ```c\n   242\t/// float c2Dot(c2v a, c2v b) {\n   243\t///     return a.x * b.x + a.y * b.y;\n   244\t/// }\n   245\t/// ```\n   246\t///\n   247\t/// GCC emits `mulss` twice with the `a` lane as destination and then\n   248\t/// `addss` with the `x` product as destination; the helpers pin that order so\n   249\t/// NaN inputs yield the same bytes.\n   250\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   251\tpub extern \"C\" fn c2Dot(a: c2v, b: c2v) -> f32 {\n   252\t    add_keep_lhs_nan(mul_keep_lhs_nan(a.x, b.x), mul_keep_lhs_nan(a.y, b.y))\n   253\t}\n   254\t\n   255\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   256\t// Collision routines\n   257\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   258\t\n   259\t/// ```c\n   260\t/// int c2CircletoCircle(c2Circle A, c2Circle B) {\n   261\t///     c2v c = c2Sub(B.p, A.p);\n   262\t///     float d2 = c2Dot(c, c);\n   263\t///     float r2 = A.r + B.r;\n   264\t///     r2 = r2 * r2;\n   265\t///     return d2 < r2;\n   266\t/// }\n   267\t/// ```\n   268\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   269\tpub extern \"C\" fn c2CircletoCircle(A: c2Circle, B: c2Circle) -> c_int {\n   270\t    let c = c2Sub(B.p, A.p);\n   271\t    let d2 = c2Dot(c, c);\n   272\t    let mut r2 = A.r + B.r;\n   273\t    r2 = r2 * r2;\n   274\t    (d2 < r2) as c_int\n   275\t}\n   276\t\n   277\t/// ```c\n   278\t/// int c2CircletoAABB(c2Circle A, c2AABB B) {\n   279\t///     c2v L = c2Clampv(A.p, B.min, B.max);\n   280\t///     c2v ab = c2Sub(A.p, L);\n   281\t///     float d2 = c2Dot(ab, ab);\n   282\t///     float r2 = A.r * A.r;\n   283\t///     return d2 < r2;\n   284\t/// }\n   285\t/// ```\n   286\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   287\tpub extern \"C\" fn c2CircletoAABB(A: c2Circle, B: c2AABB) -> c_int {\n   288\t    let L = c2Clampv(A.p, B.min, B.max);\n   289\t    let ab = c2Sub(A.p, L);\n   290\t    let d2 = c2Dot(ab, ab);\n   291\t    let r2 = A.r * A.r;\n   292\t    (d2 < r2) as c_int\n   293\t}\n   294\t\n   295\t/// ```c\n   296\t/// int c2CircletoCapsule(c2Circle A, c2Capsule B) {\n   297\t///     c2v n = c2Sub(B.b, B.a);\n   298\t///     c2v ap = c2Sub(A.p, B.a);\n   299\t///     float da = c2Dot(ap, n);\n   300\t///     float d2;\n   301\t///     if (da < 0)\n   302\t///         d2 = c2Dot(ap, ap);\n   303\t///     else {\n   304\t///         float db = c2Dot(c2Sub(A.p, B.b), n);\n   305\t///         if (db < 0) {\n   306\t///             c2v e = c2Sub(ap, c2Mulvs(n, (da / c2Dot(n, n))));\n   307\t///             d2 = c2Dot(e, e);\n   308\t///         } else {\n   309\t///             c2v bp = c2Sub(A.p, B.b);\n   310\t///             d2 = c2Dot(bp, bp);\n   311\t///         }\n   312\t///     }\n   313\t///     float r = A.r + B.r;\n   314\t///     return d2 < r * r;\n   315\t/// }\n   316\t/// ```\n   317\t///\n   318\t/// The `da / c2Dot(n, n)` division has no zero guard in the C original (a\n   319\t/// degenerate capsule with `a == b` produces inf/NaN); that is preserved.\n   320\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   321\tpub extern \"C\" fn c2CircletoCapsule(A: c2Circle, B: c2Capsule) -> c_int {\n   322\t    let n = c2Sub(B.b, B.a);\n   323\t    let ap = c2Sub(A.p, B.a);\n   324\t    let da = c2Dot(ap, n);\n   325\t    let d2: f32;\n   326\t    if da < 0.0 {\n   327\t        d2 = c2Dot(ap, ap);\n   328\t    } else {\n   329\t        let db = c2Dot(c2Sub(A.p, B.b), n);\n   330\t        if db < 0.0 {\n   331\t            let e = c2Sub(ap, c2Mulvs(n, da / c2Dot(n, n)));\n   332\t            d2 = c2Dot(e, e);\n   333\t        } else {\n   334\t            let bp = c2Sub(A.p, B.b);\n   335\t            d2 = c2Dot(bp, bp);\n   336\t        }\n   337\t    }\n   338\t    let r = A.r + B.r;\n   339\t    (d2 < r * r) as c_int\n   340\t}\n   341\t\n   342\t/// ```c\n   343\t/// int c2Collided(const void *A, const void *B, C2_TYPE typeB) {\n   344\t///     switch (typeB) {\n   345\t///         case C2_TYPE_CIRCLE:  return c2CircletoCircle(*(c2Circle *)A, *(c2Circle *)B);\n   346\t///         case C2_TYPE_AABB:    return c2CircletoAABB(*(c2Circle *)A, *(c2AABB *)B);\n   347\t///         case C2_TYPE_CAPSULE: return c2CircletoCapsule(*(c2Circle *)A, *(c2Capsule *)B);\n   348\t///         default:              return 0;\n   349\t///     }\n   350\t/// }\n   351\t/// ```\n   352\t///\n   353\t/// `A` is always reinterpreted as a `c2Circle` regardless of `typeB`, exactly\n   354\t/// as in the C original.\n   355\t///\n   356\t/// # Safety\n   357\t///\n   358\t/// `A` must point to a readable `c2Circle` and `B` to a readable object of the\n   359\t/// shape selected by `typeB`, for any `typeB` in `0..=2`.\n   360\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   361\tpub unsafe extern \"C\" fn c2Collided(A: *const c_void, B: *const c_void, typeB: c_int) -> c_int {\n   362\t    match typeB {\n   363\t        C2_TYPE_CIRCLE => c2CircletoCircle(\n   364\t            unsafe { (A as *const c2Circle).read_unaligned() },\n   365\t            unsafe { (B as *const c2Circle).read_unaligned() },\n   366\t        ),\n   367\t        C2_TYPE_AABB => c2CircletoAABB(\n   368\t            unsafe { (A as *const c2Circle).read_unaligned() },\n   369\t            unsafe { (B as *const c2AABB).read_unaligned() },\n   370\t        ),\n   371\t        C2_TYPE_CAPSULE => c2CircletoCapsule(\n   372\t            unsafe { (A as *const c2Circle).read_unaligned() },\n   373\t            unsafe { (B as *const c2Capsule).read_unaligned() },\n   374\t        ),\n   375\t        _ => 0,\n   376\t    }\n   377\t}\n   378\t\n   379\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   380\t// Public entry point (c_src/include/lib.h)\n   381\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   382\t\n   383\t/// ```c\n   384\t/// int circle_collide(float x, float y, float r);\n   385\t/// ```\n   386\t///\n   387\t/// Tests the circle `((x, y), r)` against three hard-coded shapes and packs the\n   388\t/// three boolean results into bits 0, 1 and 2 of the return value.\n   389\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   390\tpub extern \"C\" fn circle_collide(x: f32, y: f32, r: f32) -> c_int {\n   391\t    let mut result: c_int = 0;\n   392\t\n   393\t    let mut circle_in = c2Circle {\n   394\t        p: c2v { x: 0.0, y: 0.0 },\n   395\t        r: 0.0,\n   396\t    };\n   397\t    circle_in.p = c2V(x, y);\n   398\t    circle_in.r = r;\n   399\t\n   400\t    let mut circle = c2Circle {\n   401\t        p: c2v { x: 0.0, y: 0.0 },\n   402\t        r: 0.0,\n   403\t    };\n   404\t    circle.p = c2V(-70.0f32, 0.0);\n   405\t    circle.r = 20.0f32;\n   406\t\n   407\t    let mut aabb = c2AABB {\n   408\t        min: c2v { x: 0.0, y: 0.0 },\n   409\t        max: c2v { x: 0.0, y: 0.0 },\n   410\t    };\n   411\t    aabb.min = c2V(-40.0f32, -40.0f32);\n   412\t    aabb.max = c2V(-15.0f32, -15.0f32);\n   413\t\n   414\t    let mut capsule = c2Capsule {\n   415\t        a: c2v { x: 0.0, y: 0.0 },\n   416\t        b: c2v { x: 0.0, y: 0.0 },\n   417\t        r: 0.0,\n   418\t    };\n   419\t    capsule.a = c2V(-40.0f32, 40.0f32);\n   420\t    capsule.b = c2V(-20.0f32, 100.0f32);\n   421\t    capsule.r = 10.0f32;\n   422\t\n   423\t    let circle_in_p: *const c_void = (&raw const circle_in).cast();\n   424\t    let circle_p: *const c_void = (&raw const circle).cast();\n   425\t    let aabb_p: *const c_void = (&raw const aabb).cast();\n   426\t    let capsule_p: *const c_void = (&raw const capsule).cast();\n   427\t\n   428\t    result += unsafe { c2Collided(circle_in_p, circle_p, C2_TYPE_CIRCLE) };\n   429\t\n   430\t    result += unsafe { c2Collided(circle_in_p, aabb_p, C2_TYPE_AABB) } << 1;\n   431\t\n   432\t    result += unsafe { c2Collided(circle_in_p, capsule_p, C2_TYPE_CAPSULE) } << 2;\n   433\t\n   434\t    result\n   435\t}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9b90b9fb-d281-49bf-812e-b5b81b3c7dcd","uuid":"2d756b01-f4ee-41c3-bd77-13b01142f2f9","timestamp":"2026-08-27T06:36:49.979Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"int circle_collide(float x, float y, float r);\n=== RUST ===\n     1\t//! Rust translation of the C library in `c_src/`.\n     2\t//!\n     3\t//! Original C sources: `c_src/include/lib.h`, `c_src/src/lib.c`\n     4\t//! (a trimmed-down slice of `cute_c2` by Randy Gaul — zlib / Unlicense).\n     5\t//!\n     6\t//! The whole public ABI of the C shared object is reproduced here, symbol for\n     7\t//! symbol:\n     8\t//!\n     9\t//! ```text\n    10\t//! c2V  c2Mulvs  c2Maxv  c2Minv  c2Clampv  c2Sub  c2Dot\n    11\t//! c2CircletoCircle  c2CircletoAABB  c2CircletoCapsule\n    12\t//! c2Collided  circle_collide\n    13\t//! ```\n    14\t//!\n    15\t//! Notes on faithfulness:\n    16\t//! * All arithmetic is done in `f32`, matching C `float` on x86-64 (SSE, no\n    17\t//!   excess precision), so results are bit-for-bit identical.\n    18\t//! * The min/max helpers reproduce C's `a > b ? a : b` ternaries verbatim\n    19\t//!   rather than using `f32::max`/`f32::min`, because the two disagree on NaN\n    20\t//!   and signed zero.\n    21\t//! * No bugs are \"fixed\": e.g. `c2CircletoCapsule` still divides by\n    22\t//!   `c2Dot(n, n)` without a zero check, and `c2Collided` still blindly\n    23\t//!   reinterprets `A` as a `c2Circle`.\n    24\t\n    25\t#![allow(non_snake_case)]\n    26\t#![allow(non_camel_case_types)]\n    27\t\n    28\tuse core::ffi::{c_int, c_void};\n    29\t\n    30\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    31\t// Types (from c_src/src/lib.c)\n    32\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    33\t\n    34\t/// `typedef enum { C2_TYPE_CIRCLE, C2_TYPE_AABB, C2_TYPE_CAPSULE } C2_TYPE;`\n    35\t///\n    36\t/// A C enum whose enumerators all fit in `int` is passed as `int`, so the\n    37\t/// public entry point takes a `c_int` and compares against these constants.\n    38\tpub const C2_TYPE_CIRCLE: c_int = 0;\n    39\tpub const C2_TYPE_AABB: c_int = 1;\n    40\tpub const C2_TYPE_CAPSULE: c_int = 2;\n    41\t\n    42\t/// `typedef struct c2v { float x; float y; } c2v;`\n    43\t#[repr(C)]\n    44\t#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\n    45\tpub struct c2v {\n    46\t    pub x: f32,\n    47\t    pub y: f32,\n    48\t}\n    49\t\n    50\t/// `typedef struct c2Circle { c2v p; float r; } c2Circle;`\n    51\t#[repr(C)]\n    52\t#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\n    53\tpub struct c2Circle {\n    54\t    pub p: c2v,\n    55\t    pub r: f32,\n    56\t}\n    57\t\n    58\t/// `typedef struct c2AABB { c2v min; c2v max; } c2AABB;`\n    59\t#[repr(C)]\n    60\t#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\n    61\tpub struct c2AABB {\n    62\t    pub min: c2v,\n    63\t    pub max: c2v,\n    64\t}\n    65\t\n    66\t/// `typedef struct c2Capsule { c2v a; c2v b; float r; } c2Capsule;`\n    67\t#[repr(C)]\n    68\t#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\n    69\tpub struct c2Capsule {\n    70\t    pub a: c2v,\n    71\t    pub b: c2v,\n    72\t    pub r: f32,\n    73\t}\n    74\t\n    75\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    76\t// Bit-exact float multiply helpers\n    77\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    78\t//\n    79\t// IEEE-754 does not specify *which* NaN a binary operation returns, and on SSE\n    80\t// the answer is \"the destination operand, if it is a NaN, otherwise the source\n    81\t// operand\". So when both multiplicands are NaNs with different sign bits or\n    82\t// payloads, the raw result bytes depend on the operand order the compiler\n    83\t// happened to emit.\n    84\t//\n    85\t// `fmul` is commutative in LLVM IR, so plain `a * b` in Rust lets the backend\n    86\t// pick either order — and it picks the opposite of GCC's choice in `c2Dot` and\n    87\t// `c2Mulvs`. These helpers pin the order down to match the C shared object\n    88\t// byte for byte. Everything else in this file is ordinary `f32` arithmetic.\n    89\t\n    90\t/// `mulss dst, src` with `dst = a`: propagates `a`'s NaN in preference to `b`'s.\n    91\t///\n    92\t/// Matches GCC's `mulss %xmm(b),%xmm(a)` in `c2Dot`.\n    93\t///\n    94\t/// This has to be inline assembly: the `_mm_mul_ss` intrinsic lowers to an\n    95\t/// ordinary commutative LLVM `fmul`, which the backend then re-commutes right\n    96\t/// back to the order we are trying to avoid.\n    97\t#[cfg(target_arch = \"x86_64\")]\n    98\t#[inline(always)]\n    99\tfn mul_keep_lhs_nan(a: f32, b: f32) -> f32 {\n   100\t    let mut dst = a;\n   101\t    // SAFETY: `mulss` on two SSE registers has no memory or flag effects, and\n   102\t    // SSE is a baseline feature of the x86_64 target.\n   103\t    unsafe {\n   104\t        core::arch::asm!(\n   105\t            \"mulss {dst}, {src}\",\n   106\t            dst = inout(xmm_reg) dst,\n   107\t            src = in(xmm_reg) b,\n   108\t            options(pure, nomem, nostack, preserves_flags),\n   109\t        );\n   110\t    }\n   111\t    dst\n   112\t}\n   113\t\n   114\t#[cfg(not(target_arch = \"x86_64\"))]\n   115\t#[inline(always)]\n   116\tfn mul_keep_lhs_nan(a: f32, b: f32) -> f32 {\n   117\t    a * b\n   118\t}\n   119\t\n   120\t/// `addss dst, src` with `dst = a`: propagates `a`'s NaN in preference to `b`'s.\n   121\t///\n   122\t/// Matches GCC's `addss %xmm(b),%xmm(a)` in `c2Dot`.\n   123\t#[cfg(target_arch = \"x86_64\")]\n   124\t#[inline(always)]\n   125\tfn add_keep_lhs_nan(a: f32, b: f32) -> f32 {\n   126\t    let mut dst = a;\n   127\t    // SAFETY: `addss` on two SSE registers has no memory or flag effects, and\n   128\t    // SSE is a baseline feature of the x86_64 target.\n   129\t    unsafe {\n   130\t        core::arch::asm!(\n   131\t            \"addss {dst}, {src}\",\n   132\t            dst = inout(xmm_reg) dst,\n   133\t            src = in(xmm_reg) b,\n   134\t            options(pure, nomem, nostack, preserves_flags),\n   135\t        );\n   136\t    }\n   137\t    dst\n   138\t}\n   139\t\n   140\t#[cfg(not(target_arch = \"x86_64\"))]\n   141\t#[inline(always)]\n   142\tfn add_keep_lhs_nan(a: f32, b: f32) -> f32 {\n   143\t    a + b\n   144\t}\n   145\t\n   146\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   147\t// Vector helpers\n   148\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   149\t\n   150\t/// ```c\n   151\t/// c2v c2V(float x, float y) {\n   152\t///     c2v a;\n   153\t///     a.x = x;\n   154\t///     a.y = y;\n   155\t///     return a;\n   156\t/// }\n   157\t/// ```\n   158\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   159\tpub extern \"C\" fn c2V(x: f32, y: f32) -> c2v {\n   160\t    let mut a = c2v { x: 0.0, y: 0.0 };\n   161\t    a.x = x;\n   162\t    a.y = y;\n   163\t    a\n   164\t}\n   165\t\n   166\t/// ```c\n   167\t/// c2v c2Mulvs(c2v a, float b) {\n   168\t///     a.x *= b;\n   169\t///     a.y *= b;\n   170\t///     return a;\n   171\t/// }\n   172\t/// ```\n   173\t///\n   174\t/// GCC vectorises this to `mulps %xmm(a),%xmm(bbbb)` — i.e. the *broadcast\n   175\t/// scalar* is the destination, so `b`'s NaN wins over `a`'s in both lanes.\n   176\t/// `mul_keep_lhs_nan(b, ...)` reproduces that.\n   177\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   178\tpub extern \"C\" fn c2Mulvs(a: c2v, b: f32) -> c2v {\n   179\t    let mut a = a;\n   180\t    a.x = mul_keep_lhs_nan(b, a.x);\n   181\t    a.y = mul_keep_lhs_nan(b, a.y);\n   182\t    a\n   183\t}\n   184\t\n   185\t/// ```c\n   186\t/// c2v c2Maxv(c2v a, c2v b) {\n   187\t///     return c2V(((a.x) > (b.x) ? (a.x) : (b.x)),\n   188\t///             ((a.y) > (b.y) ? (a.y) : (b.y)));\n   189\t/// }\n   190\t/// ```\n   191\t///\n   192\t/// Deliberately *not* `f32::max`: C's ternary yields `b` when the comparison is\n   193\t/// unordered (NaN) and does not canonicalise `-0.0`/`+0.0`.\n   194\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   195\tpub extern \"C\" fn c2Maxv(a: c2v, b: c2v) -> c2v {\n   196\t    c2V(\n   197\t        if a.x > b.x { a.x } else { b.x },\n   198\t        if a.y > b.y { a.y } else { b.y },\n   199\t    )\n   200\t}\n   201\t\n   202\t/// ```c\n   203\t/// c2v c2Minv(c2v a, c2v b) {\n   204\t///     return c2V(((a.x) < (b.x) ? (a.x) : (b.x)),\n   205\t///             ((a.y) < (b.y) ? (a.y) : (b.y)));\n   206\t/// }\n   207\t/// ```\n   208\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   209\tpub extern \"C\" fn c2Minv(a: c2v, b: c2v) -> c2v {\n   210\t    c2V(\n   211\t        if a.x < b.x { a.x } else { b.x },\n   212\t        if a.y < b.y { a.y } else { b.y },\n   213\t    )\n   214\t}\n   215\t\n   216\t/// ```c\n   217\t/// c2v c2Clampv(c2v a, c2v lo, c2v hi) {\n   218\t///     return c2Maxv(lo, c2Minv(a, hi));\n   219\t/// }\n   220\t/// ```\n   221\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   222\tpub extern \"C\" fn c2Clampv(a: c2v, lo: c2v, hi: c2v) -> c2v {\n   223\t    c2Maxv(lo, c2Minv(a, hi))\n   224\t}\n   225\t\n   226\t/// ```c\n   227\t/// c2v c2Sub(c2v a, c2v b) {\n   228\t///     a.x -= b.x;\n   229\t///     a.y -= b.y;\n   230\t///     return a;\n   231\t/// }\n   232\t/// ```\n   233\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   234\tpub extern \"C\" fn c2Sub(a: c2v, b: c2v) -> c2v {\n   235\t    let mut a = a;\n   236\t    a.x -= b.x;\n   237\t    a.y -= b.y;\n   238\t    a\n   239\t}\n   240\t\n   241\t/// ```c\n   242\t/// float c2Dot(c2v a, c2v b) {\n   243\t///     return a.x * b.x + a.y * b.y;\n   244\t/// }\n   245\t/// ```\n   246\t///\n   247\t/// GCC emits `mulss` twice with the `a` lane as destination and then\n   248\t/// `addss` with the `x` product as destination; the helpers pin that order so\n   249\t/// NaN inputs yield the same bytes.\n   250\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   251\tpub extern \"C\" fn c2Dot(a: c2v, b: c2v) -> f32 {\n   252\t    add_keep_lhs_nan(mul_keep_lhs_nan(a.x, b.x), mul_keep_lhs_nan(a.y, b.y))\n   253\t}\n   254\t\n   255\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   256\t// Collision routines\n   257\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   258\t\n   259\t/// ```c\n   260\t/// int c2CircletoCircle(c2Circle A, c2Circle B) {\n   261\t///     c2v c = c2Sub(B.p, A.p);\n   262\t///     float d2 = c2Dot(c, c);\n   263\t///     float r2 = A.r + B.r;\n   264\t///     r2 = r2 * r2;\n   265\t///     return d2 < r2;\n   266\t/// }\n   267\t/// ```\n   268\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n   269\tpub extern \"C\" fn c2CircletoCircle(A: c2Circle, B: c2Circle) -> c_int {\n   270\t    let c = c2Sub(B.p, A.p);\n   271\t    let d2 = c2Dot(c, c);\n   272\t    let mut r2 = A.r + B.r;\n   273\t    r2 = r2 * r2;\n   274\t    (d2 < r2) as c_int\n   275\t}\n   276\t\n   277\t/// ```c\n   278\t/// int c2CircletoAABB(c2Circle A, c2