e C — and documented the reasoning inline so it doesn't look like a fudge.\n\nI also found a bug in my own `check_features.sh`: piping into `grep -q` under `set -o pipefail` made the pipeline inherit cargo's non-zero exit status, so a **failing** run reported as passing. I caught it only because I injected a deliberately-failing test to check the checker. Worth flagging as a general hazard.\n\nArtifacts: `SYMBOLS.md` (12/12, empty diff), `ERRORS.md` (42 rows), `CONFIGS.md` (59 rows), `VERIFICATION.md`, `check_features.sh`. 107 tests, each run against **both** the release and debug Rust `.so` under both feature combinations. All float comparisons are on raw bits, so `-0.0` and NaN payloads are failures. `c_src/` is untouched (md5sums recorded).","ttft_ms":2740,"ttft_stream_ms":2584,"time_to_request_ms":44,"type":"result","duration_ms":1552828,"uuid":"512d943e-b73c-4d77-b27c-a9f7c945b122","queued_turn_count":0}
